From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 12:05:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: add qdma paging and layout helpers

The per-queue qtx_* registers live in two 16-queue pages, and the v3
silicon (with the MT7988 exception) uses different rate / weight field
widths than v1/v2. Both invariants are open-coded all over the driver.

Introduce inline helpers in mtk_eth_soc.h for patches in this series:
  - mtk_qdma_select_page()   - select the page containing qid @idx
  - MTK_QTX_REG_OFS()        - per-page byte offset for qid @idx
  - mtk_qtx_sch_is_v3_layout() - true on v3 silicon except MT7988

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.h |   21 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.h
@@ -1653,5 +1653,26 @@ int mtk_flow_offload_cmd(struct mtk_eth
 void mtk_flow_offload_cleanup(struct mtk_eth *eth, struct list_head *list);
 void mtk_eth_set_dma_device(struct mtk_eth *eth, struct device *dma_dev);
 
+/* QDMA per-queue registers are paged: queues 0..15 live on page 0,
+ * 16..31 on page 1. Every access to qtx_cfg / qtx_sch / qtx_mib must
+ * be preceded by writing the page index to qdma.page; the offset
+ * within the page is (idx % MTK_QTX_PER_PAGE) * MTK_QTX_OFFSET.
+ */
+static inline void mtk_qdma_select_page(struct mtk_eth *eth, unsigned int idx)
+{
+	mtk_w32(eth, idx / MTK_QTX_PER_PAGE, eth->soc->reg_map->qdma.page);
+}
+
+#define MTK_QTX_REG_OFS(idx)	(MTK_QTX_OFFSET * ((idx) % MTK_QTX_PER_PAGE))
+
+/* Netsys v3 silicon (other than MT7988) uses the wider _V3 variants of
+ * the qtx_sch rate / weight fields. MT7988, despite being v3-class,
+ * keeps the v1/v2 layout for these fields.
+ */
+static inline bool mtk_qtx_sch_is_v3_layout(struct mtk_eth *eth)
+{
+	return mtk_is_netsys_v3_or_greater(eth) &&
+	       eth->soc->caps != MT7988_CAPS;
+}
 
 #endif /* MTK_ETH_H */
